 - Bash: mkdir -p /tmp/own && cat > /tmp/own/own.py <<'EOF'
import subprocess, sys, os, collections
repo = sys.argv[1]
files = subprocess.run(["git","-C",repo,"ls-files","-z"],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.split("\0")
res = collections.defaultdict(collections.Counter)
for f in filter(None, files):
    ext = os.path.splitext(f)[1] or os.path.basename(f)
    p = subprocess.run(["git","-C",repo,"blame","-w","--line-porcelain","-e","HEAD","--",f],capture_output=True,text=True,errors="replace")
    if p.returncode: continue
    for l in p.stdout.splitlines():
        if l.startswith("author-mail "):
            res[ext][l[12:]] += 1
for ext, c in sorted(res.items(), key=lambda x:-sum(x[1].values()
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner per extension, counted as surviving lines at HEAD with `git blame -w`:

| Ext | Lines | Top owner | Next |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 1202 | <email redacted>, 469 (39%) | fiona@formatter.example 291 (24%); <email redacted> 245 (20%) |
| `.yml` | 383 | <email redacted>, 117 (30%) | inigomarquinez 95 (24%); bjohansebas 63 (16%) |
| `.md` | 341 | <email redacted>, 116 (34%) | <email redacted> 72 (21%); doug 67 (19%) |
| `.json` | 42 | <email redacted>, 20 (47%) | troygoode 12 (28%) |
| `LICENSE` | 22 | <email redacted>, 17 (77%) | troygoode 5 (22%) |
| `.gitignore` | 5 | <email redacted>, 4 (80%) | troygoode 1 |

- **`.js`:** The latest commit, `style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes`, is by fiona@formatter.example. It gives that author 24% of `.js`. `-w` skips pure indentation changes, but that commit also changed quotes, so those lines count as theirs. Without it, troygoode's share would be higher.
- **Extensions:** Files with no extension are grouped under their file name, which is why `LICENSE` has its own row.
- **Authors:** Authors are matched by email, so one person with two emails counts as two authors.
